Template: remotedesktop-host/server-address
Type: string
Default: @DEFAULT_RENDEZVOUS_URI@
Description: Signaling server address:
 The WebSocket address of the server this machine registers with, for
 example wss://rd.example.com:5080/ws (TLS). Plain ws:// is only accepted
 for a loopback address such as ws://127.0.0.1:5080/ws; a non-loopback
 ws:// address is refused at startup unless Transport:AllowInsecureSignaling
 is set explicitly.
 .
 127.0.0.1 only reaches a server on this machine. Both machines in a
 session must be pointed at the same server.

Template: remotedesktop-host/server-certificate
Type: string
Default:
Description: Server certificate:
 Only used for a wss:// address. The PEM certificate of a server that
 uses a self-signed certificate; it is installed into this machine's
 trust store.
 .
 Leave empty if the server's certificate comes from a public authority,
 or if the address is ws://.

Template: remotedesktop-host/unattended-password
Type: password
Default:
Description: Unattended access password:
 The fixed password somebody can use to connect without a person at
 this machine's keyboard. It is stored for each user who is signed in
 when the package is configured, and must be at least 8 characters.
 .
 Leave empty to set no password on a fresh installation, or to keep the
 one already stored on an upgrade or reinstall; an empty answer never
 clears an existing password. Change it later with:
  dpkg-reconfigure remotedesktop-host
 .
 The host runs inside a graphical session. If nobody is signed in at
 installation time, the password cannot be stored; sign in and run the
 host with --set-fixed-password as that user instead.
 .
 On Linux the password lets a connection through, but the desktop
 portal still asks for control permission on every session, so an
 unattended machine can be watched but not typed into.
